This repository contains 19 task-scoped Agent Skills (`frappe-*`), with
`frappe-router` as the entry point.

Portions of the routing guidance and the terse backend/frontend reference
material are derived from the upstream Frappe skills published by Frappe
Technologies at https://github.com/frappe/skills — specifically its
`frappe-app-dev` skill (global rules, flow selection, and the initial
references for doctypes, controllers, api, database, caching, realtime,
background-jobs, hooks, permissions, testing, frontend and bench operations).
That material has since been extended by source-verified references written
against installed Frappe v16, ERPNext v16 and HRMS v16 source.

Portions are adopted from the Frappe Skills published by LUBUS at
https://github.com/lubusIN/frappe-skills, licensed MIT (full text in
LICENSES/frappe-skills-lubusIN-MIT.txt). Adopted 2026-09-23 at upstream commit
afd9ea1: the whole of its 14 skills — api-development, app-development,
desk-customization, doctype-development, enterprise-patterns, frappe-manager,
frontend-development, printing-templates, project-triage, reports, router,
testing, ui-patterns, web-forms. On 2026-09-23 this repository also adopted its
structure: the router + task-skill layout, per-skill `references/`, and the
nine-section SKILL.md format (When to use, Inputs required, Procedure,
Verification, Failure modes / debugging, Escalation, References, Guardrails,
Common Mistakes). Skill names carry a `frappe-` prefix here because they install
into a shared skill root. Blocks taken from it carry an inline
`Adopted from lubusIN/frappe-skills` provenance note naming the source file.

The frappe-ui references (frontend development, UI patterns, design tokens) are
verified against frappe-ui 1.0.0-beta.29 source (https://github.com/frappe/frappe-ui,
MIT) with 0.1.x differences noted. Parts are adapted from that repository's
`skills/frappe-ui/` agent skill, `PHILOSOPHY.md`, `CONTEXT.md` and `spec/`
documents; files that do so say so in their first lines.

Code examples cite Frappe Framework, ERPNext, HRMS, Frappe CRM and Frappe
Insights source, all published by Frappe Technologies under the GNU General
Public License v3 / MIT depending on the project. Those citations are
references for verification, not redistribution of those works.

This repository is private and not published under an open-source license.
